    "q-212506": {
      "dom_id": "step-q212506",
      "name": "Question 3",
      "problem": "Consider the following congruence.\n\n$$\n-10≡\\,(\\text{mod}\\,7)\n$$\n\nWhich of the following values gives a true statement when inserted into the blank space?\n\n- $-3$\n- $-1$\n- $4$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each case in turn.\n\n- Case I gives a true statement. Indeed, $7∣(-10-(-3)).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(-10-(-3))÷7=-7÷7=-1\n$$\n\n- Case II gives a false statement because $7∤(-10-(-1)).$ Notice that $-10-(-1)=-9,$ which is not divisible by $7.$\n\n- Case III gives a true statement. Indeed, $7∣(-10-4).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(-10-4)÷7=-14÷7=-2\n$$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$-3$ and $4$ only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
