    "q-212514": {
      "dom_id": "step-q212514",
      "name": "Question 4",
      "problem": "Consider the following congruence.\n\n$$\n-11≡\\,(\\text{mod}\\,8)\n$$\n\nWhich of the following values gives a true statement when inserted into the blank space?\n\n- $-8$\n- $5$\n- $11$",
      "worked_solution": "First, we recall that \n\n$$\na≡b\\,(\\text{mod}\\,n)\\,⟺\\,n∣(a-b).\n$$\n\nSo, $a$ and $b$ are congruent modulo $n$ if and only if $(a-b)$ is divisible by $n$ (there is no remainder).\n\nWith that in mind, let's analyze each case in turn.\n\n- Case I gives a false statement because $8∤(-11-(-8)).$ Notice that $-11-(-8)=-3,$ which is not divisible by $8.$\n\n- Case II gives a true statement. Indeed, $8∣(-11-5).$ There is no remainder:\n\n$$\n(-11-5)÷8=-16÷8=-2\n$$\n\n- Case III gives a false statement because $8∤(-11-11).$ Notice that $-11-11=-22,$ which is not divisible by $8.$\n\nTherefore, the correct answer is \"$5$ only.\"",
      "calculator_instructions": "",
      "fields": [
        {
          "key": "selection",
          "type": "radio",
          "choices": [
            {
              "option": "a",
              "dom_id": "questionWidget-choiceLetterCircle-212514-a",
              "type": "text",
              "value": "$11$ only",
